# Line-ending policy. THE INCIDENT THIS FILE EXISTS FOR (2026-07-20): git's
# autocrlf checked docker-entrypoint.sh out with CRLF on Windows, a Docker build
# ships the WORKING TREE (not the committed blob), and the image's kernel then
# failed to exec a "#!/bin/sh\r" shebang -- ENOENT crash-loop in the container
# until the file was re-written LF and redeployed. Shell scripts and anything
# a Linux container executes MUST stay LF in every checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
alembic.ini text eol=lf

# SECOND INCIDENT, 2026-07-31 (LLMemory merge train). Python is indifferent to
# CRLF, but some suites assert on RAW BYTES: verify_lqa_adjudication's mutation
# probe greps app/services/lqa.py for an anchor containing "\n", so a CRLF
# checkout fails it with "mutation anchor drifted" -- a red suite with no code
# defect. It cost three separate agents time in fresh worktrees before the
# cause was found, because `git status` is CLEAN while the bytes on disk differ
# from the committed blob. Pinning LF makes every checkout (and every
# a Docker build, which ships the working tree) byte-identical to the commit.
*.py text eol=lf

# THIRD, 2026-08-25 (G-08 dep-scanning train). CI YAML had no eol rule, so a new
# workflow authored on Windows was committed CRLF while the existing ci.yml was LF -
# a noisy whole-file diff and a CRLF-vs-LF skew in files GitHub Actions parses. Pin
# all workflow/config YAML (and the pip-audit ignore list) to LF like the rest.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
.github/pip-audit-ignores.txt text eol=lf

# Lock refreshes must preserve LF on Windows as well as Linux.
requirements*.lock text eol=lf

# Vendored axe-core (a11y train T0, test-only). Its size and sha256 are pinned by
# tests/verify_a11y_static.py (check AXE, normal sweep, no browser needed), so every
# checkout must be byte-exact (no autocrlf rewrite). `binary` also keeps the 580 KB
# minified line out of text diffs and out of the pregate secret heuristic, which
# misreads the autocomplete token table inside axe as credential assignments. Any
# change to this file therefore fails the AXE pin, not a text review.
tests/fixtures/axe/axe.min.js binary
# Hosted-instance launch kit: everything here runs in bash or a Linux container (CloudShell, Caddy).
deploy/aws-hosted/** text eol=lf

# Format batch 7: XML/DITA/DocBook round-trip fixtures are compared byte for byte.
tests/fixtures/formats/xmlits/** -text
tests/fixtures/formats/mulixml/** -text

# POSIX CLI wrapper must stay LF (a CRLF shebang cannot exec).
loc-tms text eol=lf
